Apple is planning to introduce new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> touchscreen <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> models <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/08/apple-october-27-macbook-pro/">on October 27</a> or October 28, and the machines could launch on Friday, November 6, <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> said during <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DZkRGgQn6CA">his latest podcast</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/MacBook-Pro-Ultra-Feature-1.jpg" alt="" width="2100" height="1181" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1069559" /><br/>
Apple retail stores apparently have a "big floor reset" scheduled for the evening of Thursday, November 5, and into Friday, November 6, which Gurman says could be in preparation for the new Macs. The store reset will follow a debut in late October, with Apple planning a creator-focused gathering in Los Angeles to introduce the new products.<br/>
<br/>
Along with the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; touchscreen &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;, Apple is rumored to be launching the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a>, M6 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/imac/">iMac</a>, and M6 entry-level 14-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;. Gurman did not say whether there would be a classic Apple event, but suggested Apple will "do something" and will "have those videos" at the "very least."<br/>
<br/>
Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/08/apple-planning-macbook-ultra/">previously said</a> Apple might name the new &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; Macs the "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">MacBook Ultra</a>," but he more recently walked that back and suggested they would be part of the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; line. He also said the foldable iPhone could be the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/iphone-ultra/">iPhone Ultra</a> and that Apple would debut AirPods Ultra, but so far Apple has not embraced the Ultra naming.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models could be sold as a higher-end option alongside the current mini-LED models, but new chips are not expected. Apple is said to be using the same M5 Pro and M5 Max chips that are in the existing &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models.<br/>
<br/>
